NOTES: Use an OrthographicCamera in a standard isometric-ish pose (slightly above eye level so the ring reads as an ellipse, matching the source). Build the source box with BoxGeometry plus a LineSegments EdgesGeometry black outline, and fake the source's gradient shading with a MeshLambertMaterial plus a strong directional light from upper-left. The dashed internal bore should be LineSegments with LineDashedMaterial (call computeLineDistances). Screen ring: open-ended CylinderGeometry (openEnded true) with side: THREE.DoubleSide so the pale inner surface shows, plus a thin torus or second cylinder for the top rim. Trajectory lines are Line2/LineMaterial (fat lines) so they stay visible at all zooms. Animate particles as small instanced spheres travelling along precomputed polylines: straight segment source→foil, then an instantaneous direction change at the foil, then straight to the ring wall; on arrival pulse the scintillation disc's opacity from 1→0 over ~0.6 s. Sample each particle's outcome from a weighted distribution (straight ≫ slight > large) rather than cycling deterministically, so the rarity is felt. Labels as CSS2DRenderer HTML divs with SVG/Line leader lines that fade together when labelsVisible is false. Keep OrbitControls target at the foil (+3.6, 0, 0) so orbiting spins around the scattering event; clamp polar angle to avoid going under the floor.

